{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.measure_genus_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.measure_genus_independent","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L68-L72","doc":"Corollary: the measure is genus-independent — `|χ|/(4·Area)` takes the same\nvalue `1/(8π)` at two distinct genera. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.b1_reading_coincides_iff_g4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.b1_reading_coincides_iff_g4","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L53-L66","doc":"The Betti reading `1/(π·b₁)` equals the per-loop measure `1/(8π)`\n**iff `g = 4`** — the coincidence is unique to the Bring genus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.measure_eq_gauss_bonnet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.measure_eq_gauss_bonnet","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L43-L51","doc":"The α_EM per-loop measure is the Gauss–Bonnet invariant `|χ|/(4·Area) = 1/(8π)`,\n**genus-independent**: it holds for every `g ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.loop_unit_eq_geometric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.loop_unit_eq_geometric","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L34-L41","doc":"The gauge loop unit `1/(4π)` is the geometric ratio `|χ|/(2·Area)` on any\nhyperbolic surface (`g ≠ 1`) — no QFT-correspondence input needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.b1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.b1","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L31-L32","doc":"First Betti number `b₁ = 2g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.absChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.absChi","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L28-L29","doc":"`|χ| = 2g - 2` for a genus-`g` surface (`g ≥ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.area","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmMeasureGaussBonnet.area","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmMeasureGaussBonnet.lean#L25-L26","doc":"Hyperbolic Gauss–Bonnet area of a genus-`g` surface: `Area = 4π(g-1) = -2π·χ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}